{"id": "EUVD-2026-95429", "enisaUuid": "34f90603-bc3d-324b-84fa-c269ef8425c9", "description": "HTTP/2 servers could end up crashing due to inadvertently modifying its HPACK encoder concurrently. This happens because the server modifies the HPACK encoder from two goroutines without synchronization: one uses the encoder to encode a HEADERS frame as part of a response sent to a client and the other modifies the encoder's table size when handling a SETTINGS frame containing SETTINGS_HEADER_TABLE_SIZE that a client sends. A malicious client can repeatedly send a request while changing the header table size to crash the server.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T22:54:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T15:46:39", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://go.dev/cl/847188", "https://go.dev/cl/847313", "https://go.dev/issue/81867", "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/U2fTuyDJznI", "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/ZPwCyRUuGBs", "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6617"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97032"], "assigner": "Go", "epss": 0.42, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a8810a15-e5af-3b04-b8b2-7a5f08c6425f", "product": {"name": "net/http/internal/http2", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}, "product_version": "1.27.0-0 <1.27.2"}, {"id": "bd7cd35c-d83f-36e0-a294-f1e18c99e7b9", "product": {"name": "net/http", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.26.9"}, {"id": "ff4ffb9f-b308-3349-ae47-5843f07798fa", "product": {"name": "golang.org/x/net/http2", "vendor": {"name": "golang.org/x/net"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.60.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "01d6d706-3037-3444-beb0-39b49a7c708b", "vendor": {"name": "golang.org/x/net"}}, {"id": "e5b07df9-b10f-3f84-9d9c-843a4dc620c3", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}], "isExploited": false}